{
  "title": "Create a Theme From an HTML Template | Orchard Core",
  "description": "A static HTML template is a finished design, but it has no way to manage its content. A theme keeps the design and lets Orchard Core supply the pages, the menu, and the widgets.\n\nThis video turns a template into a theme the way the built-in TheBlogTheme was made from the Clean Blog template: static assets in the wwwroot folder, named resources, a Liquid layout with zones, content templates, and an optional setup recipe.\n\nIn this video:\n• From template to theme: what you start with and what you build\n• Copy the assets\n• Declare the resources\n• Build the layout\n• Zones: where widgets appear in the layout\n• Template the content\n• A setup recipe\n• Use the theme",
